Name: Apache Portable Runtime
Short Name: apr
URL: https://github.com/apache/apr
Version: 1.5.2
Date: 2015-04-29
Revision: cff6e3232872e7f92617e291a0382c06915e28c3
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, dso, Zlib
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no
The library is not security critical because it is used for tests only.
Do not link it into production code.

Description:
   The Apache Portable Runtime Library provides a predictable and
   consistent interface to underlying platform-specific
   implementations, with an API to which software developers may code
   and be assured of predictable if not identical behavior regardless
   of the platform on which their software is built, relieving them of
   the need to code special-case conditions to work around or take
   advantage of platform-specific deficiencies or features.

Local Modifications:
src/ is a pristine checkout of the upstream Git repository at the release
tag. include/apr.h and include/arch/unix/apr_private.h are generated by
upstream's ./configure, so they are checked in outside src/. They were
generated on Linux and then edited for Android:
- apr.h: disable SCTP, SysV shared memory and semaphores, and OS UUIDs, and
  use long long for apr_int64_t and apr_uint64_t.
- apr_private.h: undefine functions and headers that Android lacks or that
  differ from glibc (accept4, dup3, epoll_create1, getifaddrs, getpass,
  nl_langinfo, pthread_mutex robust and yield, SOCK_CLOEXEC, st_*tim
  nanoseconds, sys/sem.h, sys/shm.h, uuid, glibc getservbyname_r,
  d_fileno), and getgrgid_r/getgrnam_r, which break with Android NDK r16
  and later.
